{"id":"mahabharata-5-122","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":122,"title":"द्वाविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 122 · Krishna counsels Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra tells Krishna that he agrees but cannot control his son, and asks him to persuade Duryodhana. Krishna speaks to Duryodhana gently, urging him to make peace with the Pandavas for his own sake and his family's, to heed his elders and not to be led by evil counsellors.","kn":"ತಾನು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತೇನೆ ಆದರೆ ಮಗನನ್ನು ನಿಯಂತ್ರಿಸಲಾರೆ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಒಲಿಸು ಎಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತನ್ನ ಮತ್ತು ಕುಟುಂಬದ ಹಿತಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಪಾಂಡವರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಧಿ ಮಾಡು, ಹಿರಿಯರ ಮಾತು ಕೇಳು, ದುಷ್ಟಮಂತ್ರಿಗಳ ಹಿಂದೆ ಹೋಗಬೇಡ ಎಂದು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ಮೃದುವಾಗಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र श्रीकृष्ण से कहते हैं कि वे सहमत हैं पर अपने पुत्र को वश में नहीं कर सकते, और उनसे दुर्योधन को समझाने को कहते हैं। श्रीकृष्ण कोमलता से दुर्योधन से कहते हैं कि अपने और अपने परिवार के हित के लिए पाण्डवों से सन्धि करे, बड़ों की बात माने और दुष्ट मन्त्रियों के बहकावे में न आए।","te":"తాను అంగీకరిస్తాను కానీ కుమారుని అదుపు చేయలేనని, దుర్యోధనుని ఒప్పించమని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు శ్రీకృష్ణుని అడుగుతాడు. తన, కుటుంబ హితం కోసం పాండవులతో సంధి చేసుకోమని, పెద్దల మాట వినమని, దుష్ట మంత్రుల మాటలకు లొంగవద్దని శ్రీకృష్ణుడు దుర్యోధనునికి మృదువుగా చెబుతాడు.","ta":"தான் உடன்படுகிறேன் ஆனால் மகனைக் கட்டுப்படுத்த முடியவில்லை, துரியோதனனை இணங்க வையுங்கள் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரிடம் கேட்கிறான். உனக்கும் குடும்பத்துக்கும் நன்மைக்காகப் பாண்டவர்களுடன் சமாதானம் செய், மூத்தோர் சொல் கேள், தீய ஆலோசகர்களால் வழிநடத்தப்படாதே என்று ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் துரியோதனனிடம் மென்மையாகச் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"താൻ യോജിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും, പക്ഷേ മകനെ നിയന്ത്രിക്കാനാകില്ലെന്നും ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ കൃഷ്ണനോട് പറയുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനനെ അനുനയിപ്പിക്കാൻ അദ്ദേഹം കൃഷ്ണനോട് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു. കൃഷ്ണൻ ദുര്യോധനനോട് മൃദുവായി സംസാരിക്കുന്നു; സ്വന്തം നന്മയ്ക്കും കുടുംബത്തിന്റെ നന്മയ്ക്കുമായി പാണ്ഡവരുമായി സന്ധി ചെയ്യാൻ അദ്ദേഹം ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; മുതിർന്നവരെ അനുസരിക്കാനും, ദുഷ്ടമന്ത്രിമാരുടെ വഴിയിൽ പോകാതിരിക്കാനും ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.122; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भगवन्नेवमेवैतद्यथा वदसि नारद ।\nइच्छामि चाहमप्येवं न त्वीशो भगवन्नहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Blessed Narada, it is exactly as you say, and I too wish it so, but I am not the master.'"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततः कृष्णमभ्यभाषत भारत ।\nस्वर्ग्यं लोक्यं च मामात्थ धर्म्यं न्याय्यं च केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said so, Dhritarashtra then spoke to Krishna, Bharata: 'You have told me, Keshava, what is heavenly, worldly, righteous and just."}},{"n":3,"text":"न त्वहं स्ववशस्तात क्रियमाणं न मे प्रियम् ।\nअङ्ग दुर्योधनं कृष्ण मन्दं शास्त्रातिगं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I am not in my own control, dear one, and what is done is not to my liking. Krishna, try to win over my foolish Duryodhana, who has gone beyond the teachings."}},{"n":4,"text":"अनुनेतुं महाबाहो यतस्व पुरुषोत्तम ।\nसुहृत्कार्यं तु सुमहत्कृतं ते स्याज्जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strive to do so, mighty-armed best of men; you will have done a very great service for a friend, Janardana.'"}},{"n":5,"text":"ततोऽभ्यावृत्य वार्ष्णेयो दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ।\nअब्रवीन्मधुरां वाचं सर्वधर्मार्थतत्त्ववित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Vrishni, Krishna, turned to the impatient Duryodhana and spoke sweet words, knowing the truth of all Dharma and wealth."}},{"n":6,"text":"दुर्योधन निबोधेदं मद्वाक्यं कुरुसत्तम ।\nसमर्थं ते विशेषेण सानुबन्धस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Duryodhana, best of Kurus, listen to my words, which are especially fitting for you together with your followers, Bharata."}},{"n":7,"text":"महाप्राज्ञ कुले जातः साध्वेतत्कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nश्रुतवृत्तोपसंपन्नः सर्वैः समुदितो गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born in a family of great wisdom, learned and well-conducted and endowed with all virtues, you should do what is right."}},{"n":8,"text":"दौष्कुलेया दुरात्मानो नृशंसा निरपत्रपाः ।\nत एतदीदृशं कुर्युर्यथा त्वं तात मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is the ill-born, the wicked, the cruel and the shameless who would act as you think fit, dear one."}},{"n":9,"text":"धर्मार्थयुक्ता लोकेऽस्मिन्प्रवृत्तिर्लक्ष्यते सताम् ।\nअसतां विपरीता तु लक्ष्यते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this world the conduct of the good is seen to accord with Dharma and wealth, but that of the bad is seen to be the reverse, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":10,"text":"विपरीता त्वियं वृत्तिरसकृल्लक्ष्यते त्वयि ।\nअधर्मश्चानुबन्धोऽत्र घोरः प्राणहरो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That reverse conduct is seen in you repeatedly, and it carries a terrible, great, life-destroying injustice with it."}},{"n":11,"text":"अनेकशस्त्वन्निमित्तमयशस्यं च भारत ।\nतमनर्थं परिहरन्नात्मश्रेयः करिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many times, Bharata, a dishonor has arisen because of you. By avoiding that harm, you will do what is best for yourself."}},{"n":12,"text":"भ्रातॄणामथ भृत्यानां मित्राणां च परंतप ।\nअधर्म्यादयशस्याच्च कर्मणस्त्वं प्रमोक्ष्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will free your brothers, servants and friends, scorcher of foes, from an unrighteous and disgraceful act."}},{"n":13,"text":"प्राज्ञैः शूरैर्महोत्साहैरात्मवद्भिर्बहुश्रुतैः ।\nसंधत्स्व पुरुषव्याघ्र पाण्डवैर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Make peace with the Pandavas, tiger among men, bull of the Bharatas, with the wise, the brave, the very energetic, the self-possessed and the learned."}},{"n":14,"text":"तद्धितं च प्रियं चैव धृतराष्ट्रस्य धीमतः ।\nपितामहस्य द्रोणस्य विदुरस्य महामतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That is for the good and pleasure of the wise Dhritarashtra, of the grandfather Bhishma, of Drona, of the wise Vidura,"}},{"n":15,"text":"कृपस्य सोमदत्तस्य बाह्लीकस्य च धीमतः ।\nअश्वत्थाम्नो विकर्णस्य संजयस्य विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"of Kripa, Somadatta, the wise Bahlika, Ashvatthama, Vikarna and Sanjaya, lord of men."}},{"n":16,"text":"ज्ञातीनां चैव भूयिष्ठं मित्राणां च परंतप ।\nशमे शर्म भवेत्तात सर्वस्य जगतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"And of most of your kinsmen and friends, scorcher of foes. In peace there is welfare for all, and for the whole world, dear one."}},{"n":17,"text":"ह्रीमानसि कुले जातः श्रुतवाननृशंसवान् ।\nतिष्ठ तात पितुः शास्त्रे मातुश्च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are modest, born in a good family, learned and kind. Abide by the instruction of your father and mother, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":18,"text":"एतच्छ्रेयो हि मन्यन्ते पिता यच्छास्ति भारत ।\nउत्तमापद्गतः सर्वः पितुः स्मरति शासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They think that what a father advises is best; everyone in the worst distress remembers his father's command."}},{"n":19,"text":"रोचते ते पितुस्तात पाण्डवैः सह संगमः ।\nसामात्यस्य कुरुश्रेष्ठ तत्तुभ्यं तात रोचताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father, dear one, favors a union with the Pandavas, together with his ministers. Let that please you, best of Kurus."}},{"n":20,"text":"श्रुत्वा यः सुहृदां शास्त्रं मर्त्यो न प्रतिपद्यते ।\nविपाकान्ते दहत्येनं किंपाकमिव भक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who hears the counsel of friends and does not follow it will be burned at the ripening, like one who has eaten a kimpaka fruit."}},{"n":21,"text":"यस्तु निःश्रेयसं वाक्यं मोहान्न प्रतिपद्यते ।\nस दीर्घसूत्रो हीनार्थः पश्चात्तापेन युज्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who through delusion does not follow advice that leads to the highest good becomes slow, loses his purpose and is joined to remorse afterwards."}},{"n":22,"text":"यस्तु निःश्रेयसं श्रुत्वा प्राप्तमेवाभिपद्यते ।\nआत्मनो मतमुत्सृज्य स लोके सुखमेधते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, having heard advice for the highest good, accepts it at once, giving up his own opinion, thrives happily in the world."}},{"n":23,"text":"योऽर्थकामस्य वचनं प्रातिकूल्यान्न मृष्यते ।\nशृणोति प्रतिकूलानि द्विषतां वशमेति सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, out of contrariness, will not tolerate the words of one who wishes him well, and listens to adverse things, falls under the power of his enemies."}},{"n":24,"text":"सतां मतमतिक्रम्य योऽसतां वर्तते मते ।\nशोचन्ते व्यसने तस्य सुहृदो नचिरादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who disregards the opinion of the good and follows the opinion of the bad, his friends will soon grieve over his misfortune."}},{"n":25,"text":"मुख्यानमात्यानुत्सृज्य यो निहीनान्निषेवते ।\nस घोरामापदं प्राप्य नोत्तारमधिगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who abandons principal ministers and serves the lowly, on meeting a terrible calamity finds no deliverance."}},{"n":26,"text":"योऽसत्सेवी वृथाचारो न श्रोता सुहृदां सदा ।\nपरान्वृणीते स्वान्द्वेष्टि तं गौः शपति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who serves the bad, acts in vain, and never listens to friends, who chooses outsiders and hates his own: the very cow curses him, Bharata."}},{"n":27,"text":"स त्वं विरुध्य तैर्वीरैरन्येभ्यस्त्राणमिच्छसि ।\nअशिष्टेभ्योऽसमर्थेभ्यो मूढेभ्यो भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made enemies of those heroes, you seek protection from others, from the ill-behaved, the powerless and the foolish, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":28,"text":"को हि शक्रसमाञ्ज्ञातीनतिक्रम्य महारथान् ।\nअन्येभ्यस्त्राणमाशंसेत्त्वदन्यो भुवि मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man on earth but you would pass over kinsmen who are great chariot-warriors, equal to Indra, and look for protection from others?"}},{"n":29,"text":"जन्मप्रभृति कौन्तेया नित्यं विनिकृतास्त्वया ।\nन च ते जातु कुप्यन्ति धर्मात्मानो हि पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From birth, the sons of Kunti have always been wronged by you, and yet the righteous Pandavas never get angry."}},{"n":30,"text":"मिथ्याप्रचरितास्तात जन्मप्रभृति पाण्डवाः ।\nत्वयि सम्यङ्महाबाहो प्रतिपन्ना यशस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, dear one, have been falsely treated since birth, yet, mighty-armed, those glorious ones have behaved rightly toward you."}},{"n":31,"text":"त्वयापि प्रतिपत्तव्यं तथैव भरतर्षभ ।\nस्वेषु बन्धुषु मुख्येषु मा मन्युवशमन्वगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should behave likewise toward them, bull of the Bharatas. Do not fall under the sway of anger toward your own chief kinsmen."}},{"n":32,"text":"त्रिवर्गयुक्ता प्राज्ञानामारम्भा भरतर्षभ ।\nधर्मार्थावनुरुध्यन्ते त्रिवर्गासंभवे नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The undertakings of the wise, bull of the Bharatas, are joined to the three aims of life; if all three cannot be had, men follow Dharma and wealth."}},{"n":33,"text":"पृथक्तु विनिविष्टानां धर्मं धीरोऽनुरुध्यते ।\nमध्यमोऽर्थं कलिं बालः काममेवानुरुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they are set apart, the steadfast follow Dharma, the middling wealth, and the foolish, in strife, only desire."}},{"n":34,"text":"इन्द्रियैः प्रसृतो लोभाद्धर्मं विप्रजहाति यः ।\nकामार्थावनुपायेन लिप्समानो विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who, spread out through the senses, abandons Dharma out of greed, and seeks desire and wealth by improper means, is destroyed."}},{"n":35,"text":"कामार्थौ लिप्समानस्तु धर्ममेवादितश्चरेत् ।\nन हि धर्मादपैत्यर्थः कामो वापि कदाचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who seeks desire and wealth should practice Dharma first; for neither wealth nor desire ever departs from Dharma."}},{"n":36,"text":"उपायं धर्ममेवाहुस्त्रिवर्गस्य विशां पते ।\nलिप्समानो हि तेनाशु कक्षेऽग्निरिव वर्धते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say that Dharma alone is the means to the three aims, lord of men; one who seeks by it grows swiftly, like fire in dry grass."}},{"n":37,"text":"स त्वं तातानुपायेन लिप्ससे भरतर्षभ ।\nआधिराज्यं महद्दीप्तं प्रथितं सर्वराजसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet you, dear one, seek by improper means, bull of the Bharatas, a great, blazing, sovereign rule renowned among all kings."}},{"n":38,"text":"आत्मानं तक्षति ह्येष वनं परशुना यथा ।\nयः सम्यग्वर्तमानेषु मिथ्या राजन्प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who acts falsely toward those who behave rightly hews himself, like a man cutting a forest with an axe, king."}},{"n":39,"text":"न तस्य हि मतिं छिन्द्याद्यस्य नेच्छेत्पराभवम् ।\nअविच्छिन्नस्य धीरस्य कल्याणे धीयते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not cut down the mind of one whose defeat one does not wish; the mind of the unbroken, steadfast man is set on good."}},{"n":40,"text":"त्यक्तात्मानं न बाधेत त्रिषु लोकेषु भारत ।\nअप्यन्यं प्राकृतं किंचित्किमु तान्पाण्डवर्षभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one in the three worlds, Bharata, should harm one who has abandoned himself, even any ordinary person, let alone those bulls of the Pandavas."}},{"n":41,"text":"अमर्षवशमापन्नो न किंचिद्बुध्यते नरः ।\nछिद्यते ह्याततं सर्वं प्रमाणं पश्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who has come under the sway of rage understands nothing. Everything stretched out is cut off; look at the evidence, Bharata."}},{"n":42,"text":"श्रेयस्ते दुर्जनात्तात पाण्डवैः सह संगमः ।\nतैर्हि संप्रीयमाणस्त्वं सर्वान्कामानवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Union with the Pandavas is better for you, dear one, than with the wicked. Pleased with them, you will obtain all your desires."}},{"n":43,"text":"पाण्डवैर्निर्जितां भूमिं भुञ्जानो राजसत्तम ।\nपाण्डवान्पृष्ठतः कृत्वा त्राणमाशंससेऽन्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enjoying the land conquered by the Pandavas, best of kings, you put the Pandavas behind you and look for protection elsewhere."}},{"n":44,"text":"दुःशासने दुर्विषहे कर्णे चापि ससौबले ।\nएतेष्वैश्वर्यमाधाय भूतिमिच्छसि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Duhshasana, who is hard to bear, in Karna and in Shakuni with his son, you place your sovereignty and seek prosperity, Bharata."}},{"n":45,"text":"न चैते तव पर्याप्ता ज्ञाने धर्मार्थयोस्तथा ।\nविक्रमे चाप्यपर्याप्ताः पाण्डवान्प्रति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are no match for you in the knowledge of Dharma and wealth, and they are no match for the Pandavas in prowess, Bharata."}},{"n":46,"text":"न हीमे सर्वराजानः पर्याप्ताः सहितास्त्वया ।\nक्रुद्धस्य भीमसेनस्य प्रेक्षितुं मुखमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these kings together with you are not enough even to look at the face of angry Bhimasena in battle."}},{"n":47,"text":"इदं संनिहितं तात समग्रं पार्थिवं बलम् ।\nअयं भीष्मस्तथा द्रोणः कर्णश्चायं तथा कृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here is the whole royal army assembled, dear one: here Bhishma, Drona, Karna and Kripa,"}},{"n":48,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः सौमदत्तिरश्वत्थामा जयद्रथः ।\nअशक्ताः सर्व एवैते प्रतियोद्धुं धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Somadatta's son, Ashvatthama and Jayadratha. All of these are unable to fight Dhananjaya in return."}},{"n":49,"text":"अजेयो ह्यर्जुनः क्रुद्धः सर्वैरपि सुरासुरैः ।\nमानुषैरपि गन्धर्वैर्मा युद्धे चेत आधिथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angry Arjuna cannot be conquered by all the gods and Asuras, by men or gandharvas. Do not set your mind on battle."}},{"n":50,"text":"दृश्यतां वा पुमान्कश्चित्समग्रे पार्थिवे बले ।\nयोऽर्जुनं समरे प्राप्य स्वस्तिमानाव्रजेद्गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Show me any man in the whole royal army who, meeting Arjuna in battle, would come home safe."}},{"n":51,"text":"किं ते जनक्षयेणेह कृतेन भरतर्षभ ।\nयस्मिञ्जिते जितं ते स्यात्पुमानेकः स दृश्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What do you gain here by the destruction of men, bull of the Bharatas? Show me the one man whom, if defeated, you would have defeated."}},{"n":52,"text":"यः स देवान्सगन्धर्वान्सयक्षासुरपन्नगान् ।\nअजयत्खाण्डवप्रस्थे कस्तं युध्येत मानवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who among men would fight him who conquered the gods with gandharvas, yakshas, Asuras and serpents at Khandavaprastha?"}},{"n":53,"text":"तथा विराटनगरे श्रूयते महदद्भुतम् ।\nएकस्य च बहूनां च पर्याप्तं तन्निदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise, a great marvel is heard of at Virata's city; that is enough of an example for one against many."}},{"n":54,"text":"तमजेयमनाधृष्यं विजेतुं जिष्णुमच्युतम् ।\nआशंससीह समरे वीरमर्जुनमूर्जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You hope here in battle to conquer the hero Arjuna, the mighty, victorious and unfallen, who is invincible and unassailable."}},{"n":55,"text":"मद्द्वितीयं पुनः पार्थं कः प्रार्थयितुमर्हति ।\nयुद्धे प्रतीपमायान्तमपि साक्षात्पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who could seek to fight Partha when he has me as his second? Even Indra himself, coming against him in battle, could not."}},{"n":56,"text":"बाहुभ्यामुद्धरेद्भूमिं दहेत्क्रुद्ध इमाः प्रजाः ।\nपातयेत्त्रिदिवाद्देवान्योऽर्जुनं समरे जयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who would defeat Arjuna in battle could lift the earth with his arms, burn these creatures in anger, and throw the gods down from heaven."}},{"n":57,"text":"पश्य पुत्रांस्तथा भ्रातॄञ्ज्ञातीन्संबन्धिनस्तथा ।\nत्वत्कृते न विनश्येयुरेते भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at your sons, your brothers, kinsmen and relatives; let them not perish because of you, best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":58,"text":"अस्तु शेषं कौरवाणां मा पराभूदिदं कुलम् ।\nकुलघ्न इति नोच्येथा नष्टकीर्तिर्नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let a remnant of the Kauravas remain; let this family not be undone. Do not be called a destroyer of your family, king, with your fame lost."}},{"n":59,"text":"त्वामेव स्थापयिष्यन्ति यौवराज्ये महारथाः ।\nमहाराज्ये च पितरं धृतराष्ट्रं जनेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great chariot-warriors will install you as crown prince and your father Dhritarashtra, lord of men, as great king."}},{"n":60,"text":"मा तात श्रियमायान्तीमवमंस्थाः समुद्यताम् ।\nअर्धं प्रदाय पार्थेभ्यो महतीं श्रियमाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dear one, do not scorn Fortune when she comes and is ready. By giving the Pandavas half, you will gain great fortune."}},{"n":61,"text":"पाण्डवैः संशमं कृत्वा कृत्वा च सुहृदां वचः ।\nसंप्रीयमाणो मित्रैश्च चिरं भद्राण्यवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made peace with the Pandavas and having done as your friends say, you will long enjoy good things, delighting along with your friends.'"}}]}]}